<title>GREECE: Expiries of Greek T-bills, FRNs in November.</title>
<headline>Expiries of Greek T-bills, FRNs in November.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Information on expiring three-, six- and 12-month T-bills and state floating rate notes in November follows:</p>
<p>			     T-BILLS</p>
<p>  ISSUE     MATURITY   INTEREST    AMOUNT (no interest included)</p>
<p> May-2, 96   Nov-4	12.60%     48 bln drachmas</p>
<p>				FRNs</p>
<p>  ISSUE     MATURITY   LAST COUPON  SPREAD  AMOUNT(principal)</p>
<p> Nov-15, 93  Nov-15    15.15%	  1.25%   1.1 bln drachmas</p>
<p> Nov-30, 93  Nov-30    15.15%	  1.25%   8.3 bln drachmas</p>
<p> Nov-30, 92  Nov-30    15.4%	   1.50%   120 million drachmas</p>
<p>It should be noted that T-bill expiries amount to 353 billion drachmas today. Three-year FRN expiries amount to 7.0 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>All amounts have been rounded off. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
